          "text": "Momentum: \\(\\mathrm{kg\\cdot m/s}\\)",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This is a correct SI unit for momentum, so selecting it would confuse a valid derived unit with an invalid one."
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "text": "Pressure: \\(\\mathrm{N/m}\\)",
          "is_correct": true,
          "explanation": "This is the incorrect unit because pressure is force per area, not force per length. The SI unit of pressure is \\(\\mathrm{Pa}=\\mathrm{N/m^2}\\), so \\(\\mathrm{N/m}\\) has the wrong dimensions."
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "text": "Power: watt",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This is correct because the SI unit of power is the watt \\((\\mathrm{W})\\)."
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "Acceleration: \\(\\mathrm{m/s^2}\\)",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This is the standard SI unit of acceleration, so it is not the incorrect choice."
