    {
      "source_id": "11",
      "stem": "A constant force \\(\\vec F=(5.2\\,\\mathrm{N})\\hat{i}-(1.7\\,\\mathrm{N})\\hat{j}\\) acts on a particle as it moves along the \\(x\\)-axis from \\(x=1.1\\,\\mathrm{m}\\) to \\(x=3.6\\,\\mathrm{m}\\). What is the work done by the force on the particle?",
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "text": "\\(17.4\\,\\mathrm{J}\\)",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This likely uses the magnitude of the full force vector as if both components contributed to work, even though there is no \\(y\\)-displacement."
        },
