          "key": "B",
          "text": "\\(-4.25\\,\\mathrm{J}\\)",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This incorrectly uses the \\(y\\)-component of force, which does no work because the displacement has no \\(y\\)-component."
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "text": "\\(13.0\\,\\mathrm{J}\\)",
          "is_correct": true,
          "explanation": "Work is the dot product \\(W=\\vec F\\cdot \\Delta \\vec r\\). Since the particle moves only along \\(x\\), \\(\\Delta x=3.6-1.1=2.5\\,\\mathrm{m}\\) and \\(W=F_x\\Delta x=(5.2\\,\\mathrm{N})(2.5\\,\\mathrm{m})=13.0\\,\\mathrm{J}\\)."
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "\\(3.5\\,\\mathrm{J}\\)",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This arises from an arithmetic or subtraction error rather than applying \\(W=F_x\\Delta x\\) correctly."
        }
      ],
      "question_type": "multiple_choice",
      "skipped": false,
      "skip_reason": "",
      "answer": "",
      "parts": []
