          "key": "C",
          "text": "\\(72\\,\\mathrm{N}\\)",
          "is_correct": true,
          "explanation": "Use the impulse-momentum theorem: \\(F_{\\text{avg}}=\\dfrac{\\Delta p}{\\Delta t}=\\dfrac{m(v_f-v_i)}{\\Delta t}\\). Taking the initial direction as positive gives \\(v_i=+4.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s}\\) and \\(v_f=-2.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s}\\), so \\(|\\Delta v|=6.0\\,\\mathrm{m/s}\\) and \\(|F_{\\text{avg}}|=\\dfrac{(3.0)(6.0)}{0.25}=72\\,\\mathrm{N}\\)."
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "None of the above is correct.",
          "is_correct": false,
          "explanation": "This is false because option C matches the correct impulse calculation."
        }
      ],
      "question_type": "multiple_choice",
      "skipped": false,
      "skip_reason": "",
      "answer": "",
